<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Graner & Glazier (1992) / Glazier & Graner (1993) extended large-Q Cellular Potts Model cell sorting + Ouchi et al. (2003) cortical tension (Hydra attenuata (endoderm/ectoderm reaggregates) & Gallus gallus embryonic cell spheroids)" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-6> ;
    schema:about "Hydra attenuata (endoderm/ectoderm reaggregates) & Gallus gallus embryonic cell spheroids" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not model subcellular cytoskeletal actin-myosin turnover, active chemotactic signaling, cell growth/division, or 3D aggregates; does not reproduce Glazier & Graner (1993) quantitative boundary-length curves at the paper's cell size (V_t ~ 40) or run length (10^4 MCS).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 2D extended large-Q Cellular Potts Model (60 x 60 lattice, 60 cells of V_t = 16) across all 4 canonical phase regimes plus T=0 pinning and equal-adhesion negative controls, a 7-point continuous J_LD sweep, and a 6-point fluctuation temperature sweep (all at lambda_P = 0).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Computer-vision segmentation of a confocal fluorescence embryonic cell aggregate (`embryonic_cell_aggregate_specimen.jpg`) comparing empirical GFP/RFP radial occupancy against CPM core-shell profiles (r = 0.961, RMSE = 0.154).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Ouchi et al. (2003) perimeter / cortical tension term with incremental 8-neighbour bond-count bookkeeping (max drift 0 after 150 MCS), a cortical-tension sorting regime (lambda_P = 2, P_t = 44), a 6-point lambda_P ablation sweep at T = 10 and T = 80, and a 5-point P_t sweep (32-56) with realised-perimeter tracking r = 0.9999.",
        "reported_in_source: Glazier & Graner (1993) PRE Table I & Section III.B: classification of 4 equilibrium phase regimes (complete engulfment, partial sorting lens, checkerboard mixing, and cell dissociation) and fluctuation temperature controls (T=0 lattice pinning arrest vs optimal thermal sorting vs high-T thermal melting).",
        "reported_in_source: Graner & Glazier (1992) PRL Eqs. 1-3 & Fig. 3: extended large-Q Cellular Potts Model Hamiltonian with bond-energy surface tensions gamma_LD = J_LD - (J_LL + J_DD)/2 and gamma_alphaM = J_alphaM - J_alphaalpha/2 driving logarithmic heterotypic boundary decay L_het(t) ~ A - B ln(t).",
        "reported_in_source: Ouchi et al. (2003) Physica A Eq. 2: a perimeter (cortical tension) elasticity term lambda_P (p_sigma - P_t)^2 added to the CPM Hamiltonian suppresses ragged, fragmented cell boundaries; Farhadifar et al. (2007) Eq. 1 is the vertex-model analogue.",
        "transfer_boundary: 2D lattice Cellular Potts representation of 3D multicellular spheroid cross-sections; the specimen is an embryoid-body spheroid, not a Hydra reaggregate, and its core/shell labels are assigned by fluorescence channel, not by cell type.",
        "transfer_boundary: Cells equilibrate at ~76 % of V_t under lambda = 1.2 and a hard v >= 6 floor; the PRL Fig. 3 comparison uses 0-150 MCS checkpoints whose digitisation from the 10^4-MCS figure is not documented.",
        "transfer_boundary: Sorting dynamics include a whole-cell identity-swap move (8 attempts/MCS, Metropolis at 2.5 T) that is not part of the Graner-Glazier single-site copy formalism; the 'partial sorting lens' regime adds an uncited lateral bias field inside that move. Both are disclosed here, not in the script." ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0378-4371(03)00574-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2007.11.049>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/newbio239098a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.47.2128>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.69.2013>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.141.3579.401>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.122.5.1611> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-audit-v3-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-audit-v3-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-10>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-audit-v3-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-11>,
