<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting> a pk1:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Graner & Glazier (1992) / Glazier & Graner (1993) extended large-Q Cellular Potts Model cell sorting + Ouchi et al. (2003) cortical tension (Hydra attenuata (endoderm/ectoderm reaggregates) & Gallus gallus embryonic cell spheroids)",
        "Graner & Glazier (1992) / Glazier & Graner (1993) extended large-Q Cellular Potts Model cell sorting + Ouchi et al. (2003) cortical tension faithfully reproduces Hydra attenuata (endoderm/ectoderm reaggregates) & Gallus gallus embryonic cell spheroids morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-6> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Hydra attenuata (endoderm/ectoderm reaggregates) & Gallus gallus embryonic cell spheroids specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 84.5/100, audit 2026-10-19-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py> ;
    schema:about "Hydra attenuata (endoderm/ectoderm reaggregates) & Gallus gallus embryonic cell spheroids" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not model subcellular cytoskeletal actin-myosin turnover, active chemotactic signaling, cell growth/division, or 3D aggregates; does not reproduce Glazier & Graner (1993) quantitative boundary-length curves at the paper's cell size (V_t ~ 40) or run length (10^4 MCS).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 2D extended large-Q Cellular Potts Model (60 x 60 lattice, 60 cells of V_t = 16) across all 4 canonical phase regimes plus T=0 pinning and equal-adhesion negative controls, a 7-point continuous J_LD sweep, and a 6-point fluctuation temperature sweep (all at lambda_P = 0).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Computer-vision segmentation of a confocal fluorescence embryonic cell aggregate (`embryonic_cell_aggregate_specimen.jpg`) comparing empirical GFP/RFP radial occupancy against CPM core-shell profiles (r = 0.961, RMSE = 0.154).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Ouchi et al. (2003) perimeter / cortical tension term with incremental 8-neighbour bond-count bookkeeping (max drift 0 after 150 MCS), a cortical-tension sorting regime (lambda_P = 2, P_t = 44), a 6-point lambda_P ablation sweep at T = 10 and T = 80, and a 5-point P_t sweep (32-56) with realised-perimeter tracking r = 0.9999.",
        "reported_in_source: Glazier & Graner (1993) PRE Table I & Section III.B: classification of 4 equilibrium phase regimes (complete engulfment, partial sorting lens, checkerboard mixing, and cell dissociation) and fluctuation temperature controls (T=0 lattice pinning arrest vs optimal thermal sorting vs high-T thermal melting).",
        "reported_in_source: Graner & Glazier (1992) PRL Eqs. 1-3 & Fig. 3: extended large-Q Cellular Potts Model Hamiltonian with bond-energy surface tensions gamma_LD = J_LD - (J_LL + J_DD)/2 and gamma_alphaM = J_alphaM - J_alphaalpha/2 driving logarithmic heterotypic boundary decay L_het(t) ~ A - B ln(t).",
        "reported_in_source: Ouchi et al. (2003) Physica A Eq. 2: a perimeter (cortical tension) elasticity term lambda_P (p_sigma - P_t)^2 added to the CPM Hamiltonian suppresses ragged, fragmented cell boundaries; Farhadifar et al. (2007) Eq. 1 is the vertex-model analogue.",
        "transfer_boundary: 2D lattice Cellular Potts representation of 3D multicellular spheroid cross-sections; the specimen is an embryoid-body spheroid, not a Hydra reaggregate, and its core/shell labels are assigned by fluorescence channel, not by cell type.",
        "transfer_boundary: Cells equilibrate at ~76 % of V_t under lambda = 1.2 and a hard v >= 6 floor; the PRL Fig. 3 comparison uses 0-150 MCS checkpoints whose digitisation from the 10^4-MCS figure is not documented.",
        "transfer_boundary: Sorting dynamics include a whole-cell identity-swap move (8 attempts/MCS, Metropolis at 2.5 T) that is not part of the Graner-Glazier single-site copy formalism; the 'partial sorting lens' regime adds an uncited lateral bias field inside that move. Both are disclosed here, not in the script." ;
    pk1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py; output: docs/media/cellular_potts_cell_sorting_comparison.png; organism: Hydra attenuata (endoderm/ectoderm reaggregates) & Gallus gallus embryonic cell spheroids; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/654cd6fc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 7cdd3f38f0e6192e614f25f3f47d81cb4d09870705b0e0dca1d1d4dbca9f4cc0; artifact_sha256: a2f5372c202e946ae397351314585b49d1db212e3088826bfc3b642308249496; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Graner & Glazier (1992) PRL Eqs. 1-3 & Fig. 3: extended large-Q Cellular Potts Model Hamiltonian with bond-energy surface tensions gamma_LD = J_LD - (J_LL + J_DD)/2 and gamma_alphaM = J_alphaM - J_alphaalpha/2 driving logarithmic heterotypic boundary decay L_het(t) ~ A - B ln(t). | Glazier & Graner (1993) PRE Table I & Section III.B: classification of 4 equilibrium phase regimes (complete engulfment, partial sorting lens, checkerboard mixing, and cell dissociation) and fluctuation temperature controls (T=0 lattice pinning arrest vs optimal thermal sorting vs high-T thermal melting). | Ouchi et al. (2003) Physica A Eq. 2: a perimeter (cortical tension) elasticity term lambda_P (p_sigma - P_t)^2 added to the CPM Hamiltonian suppresses ragged, fragmented cell boundaries; Farhadifar et al. (2007) Eq. 1 is the vertex-model analogue.; reconstructed_in_script: 2D extended large-Q Cellular Potts Model (60 x 60 lattice, 60 cells of V_t = 16) across all 4 canonical phase regimes plus T=0 pinning and equal-adhesion negative controls, a 7-point continuous J_LD sweep, and a 6-point fluctuation temperature sweep (all at lambda_P = 0). | Ouchi et al. (2003) perimeter / cortical tension term with incremental 8-neighbour bond-count bookkeeping (max drift 0 after 150 MCS), a cortical-tension sorting regime (lambda_P = 2, P_t = 44), a 6-point lambda_P ablation sweep at T = 10 and T = 80, and a 5-point P_t sweep (32-56) with realised-perimeter tracking r = 0.9999. | Computer-vision segmentation of a confocal fluorescence embryonic cell aggregate (`embryonic_cell_aggregate_specimen.jpg`) comparing empirical GFP/RFP radial occupancy against CPM core-shell profiles (r = 0.961, RMSE = 0.154).; transfer_boundary: 2D lattice Cellular Potts representation of 3D multicellular spheroid cross-sections; the specimen is an embryoid-body spheroid, not a Hydra reaggregate, and its core/shell labels are assigned by fluorescence channel, not by cell type. | Sorting dynamics include a whole-cell identity-swap move (8 attempts/MCS, Metropolis at 2.5 T) that is not part of the Graner-Glazier single-site copy formalism; the 'partial sorting lens' regime adds an uncited lateral bias field inside that move. Both are disclosed here, not in the script. | Cells equilibrate at ~76 % of V_t under lambda = 1.2 and a hard v >= 6 floor; the PRL Fig. 3 comparison uses 0-150 MCS checkpoints whose digitisation from the 10^4-MCS figure is not documented.; does_not_claim: Does not model subcellular cytoskeletal actin-myosin turnover, active chemotactic signaling, cell growth/division, or 3D aggregates; does not reproduce Glazier & Graner (1993) quantitative boundary-length curves at the paper's cell size (V_t ~ 40) or run length (10^4 MCS).]" ;
