<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Graner & Glazier (1992) / Glazier & Graner (1993) extended large-Q Cellular Potts Model cell sorting + Ouchi et al. (2003) cortical tension — Code-to-model traceability: 83/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: the module docstring (L1-43) maps every Hamiltonian term, tension relation, regime inequality and the Pass 3 perimeter term to PRL/PRE/Physica A equation numbers and to the Lean declarations; `compute_cpm_tensions`, `square_block_perimeter_8nbr`, `perimeter_energy_delta` and `simulate_cpm_regime` docstrings name the matching Lean theorems; the math_kg loop file registers 6 equations with single-range code loci (re-pinned this pass). Deductions: the identity-swap block is labelled 'Thermally activated cell-neighbor rearrangement moves' citing §III.B (L467-468), which describes thermal boundary fluctuations, not whole-cell identity exchange — the comment misattributes a non-paper mechanism to the paper (-6); the constants 1.8 (lateral bias), 2.5 T (swap temperature), 6 (volume floor), 1.5 (trials per boundary site) and the 17.8 px seeding radius carry no comment or citation (-4); `depinning_prob` is documented in a comment (L451-453) as the pinning activation factor but never used, so the docstring's §III.B pinning explanation is not what the code does (-3); the Section 2 header still says 'Graner & Glazier 1992' although the kernel contains the swap move and the Ouchi term (-1); `is_partial` branches on the classifier string, coupling the regime label to the dynamics (-1 net of the honest lambda_P = 0 disclosure in the docstring)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py L467–L500: Swap block attributed to Glazier & Graner §III.B; uncited constants 1.8, 2.5 T <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py#L467-L500>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.3e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Graner & Glazier (1992) / Glazier & Graner (1993) extended large-Q Cellular Potts Model cell sorting + Ouchi et al. (2003) cortical tension — Model fidelity to source: 76/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: the surface tension relations (`compute_cpm_tensions`, L109-154) match PRL Eqs. 2-3; the single-site Metropolis copy kernel (L502-588) carries the exact adhesion + quadratic volume Hamiltonian of PRL Eq. 1 with the Glazier & Graner (1993) Eq. 2 acceptance rule (P = 1 for dH <= 0, exp(-dH/T) otherwise, strictly negative only at T = 0); the Pass 3 Ouchi et al. (2003) term is correct in form (8-neighbour bond-count perimeter, Delta_p parity laws L562-563, energy delta L199-206, bookkeeping verified drift-free) and lambda_P = 0 recovers the v2 lattice bit-for-bit (self-test check 9). Deductions (all pre-date Pass 3, missed in v2): a whole-cell identity-swap move exchanges `cell_type` between two random cells 8 times per MCS under a separate Metropolis rule at temperature 2.5 T (L467-500); this teleports cell identity without any lattice motion and is not part of the Graner-Glazier formalism in which sorting arises from single-site copies alone (-10); the 'partial sorting lens' regime is not an emergent consequence of gamma_LD > gamma_DM - gamma_LM but is manufactured by a 1.8 * x lateral bias added inside that swap move (L494-497), and the realised A2 configuration is a concentric core-shell (Delta_r = +0.352, centroid offset 0.21), not a lens (-5); cells equilibrate at mean v = 12.1 = 75.6 % of V_t (RMS 5.16) because lambda = 1.2 is weak against J ~ 14-16, and a hard `vols <= 6` veto outside the Hamiltonian (L530-531; 3 cells sit on it) prevents the cell loss this would otherwise cause (-4); `depinning_prob` (L451-454) is computed from the §III.B pinning argument and never used, so the T = 0 arrest is a property of the acceptance rule, not of the documented factor (-2); lattice edges are excluded from copy attempts (L524-525) so medium contact at the boundary is never sampled (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py L451–L454: depinning_prob computed and never used (dead code) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py#L451-L454>",
        "1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py L467–L500: Whole-cell cell_type identity swap, 8 attempts per MCS, own Metropolis rule at 2.5 T — not in the Graner-Glazier single-site formalism <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py#L467-L500>",
        "1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py L494–L497: is_partial lateral bias 1.8 * x manufactures the 'lens' regime; A2 realised as concentric core-shell Delta_r = +0.352 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py#L494-L497>",
        "1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py L530–L531: Hard vols <= 6 veto outside the Hamiltonian; cells at 75.6 % of V_t with 3 cells on the floor <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py#L530-L531>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 7.6e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Graner & Glazier (1992) / Glazier & Graner (1993) extended large-Q Cellular Potts Model cell sorting + Ouchi et al. (2003) cortical tension — Morphometric validation: 85/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: `measure_morphoeval()` (L1265-1391) returns 15 measurements with non-null references and units, including the 7 new Pass 3 metrics (P_t = 44 vs Lean, RMS(p - P_t) 1.73 vs the lambda_P = 0 baseline 14.05, shape index 12.30 vs the square's 11.0, fragmented fraction 0.083 vs 0, cortical Delta_r +0.355 vs +0.332, monotone RMS over the lambda_P sweep, P_t tracking r = 0.9999); the morphometrics (L238-359) compute heterotypic boundary fraction, envelopment, radial separation, volume and perimeter statistics and 12-annulus profiles; the log-decay fit gives r = -0.946. Deductions: the PRL Fig. 3 'checkpoint concordance' r = 0.972 is against five `empirical_mcs_checkpoints` (0-150 MCS, het fraction 0.48 -> 0.15) in the reference JSON that carry no digitisation provenance — the paper's Fig. 3 spans ~10^4 MCS for V_t ~ 40 cells, so these are at best rescaled and at worst invented, and the comparison is not a validation against the paper (-7); four of the new references are self-referential (the lambda_P = 0 run or the sweep's own values) rather than literature values, and the shape index reference 11.0 is a geometric constant, not a measured cell shape (-4); the mean cell volume (75.6 % of V_t) is computed but not reported as a measurement with reference V_t (-2); no measurement of the swap-move contribution to sorting exists, so the reported Delta_r cannot be attributed to the Hamiltonian (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py L1349–L1355: cortical_tension_rms_perimeter_deviation reference_value is the script's own lambda_P = 0 run (self-referential) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py#L1349-L1355>",
        "datasets/cellular_potts_cell_sorting/cellular_potts_cell_sorting_reference.json L169–L180: PRL Fig. 3 'empirical_mcs_checkpoints' at 0-150 MCS with no digitisation provenance; the paper's figure spans ~10^4 MCS <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/datasets/cellular_potts_cell_sorting/cellular_potts_cell_sorting_reference.json#L169-L180>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-measurement-checkerboard-mixing-heterotypic-boundary-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-measurement-complete-sorting-heterotypic-boundary-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-measurement-complete-sorting-radial-core-shell-separation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-measurement-cortical-tension-fragmented-cell-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-measurement-cortical-tension-rms-perimeter-deviation>,
