<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Graner & Glazier (1992) / Glazier & Graner (1993) extended large-Q Cellular Potts Model cell sorting + Ouchi et al. (2003) cortical tension — MorphoEval overall 84.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py` (84.5/100, down from 91.1/100 in Pass 2). The single v2 remediation item is closed: the Ouchi et al. (2003) perimeter elasticity term lambda_P (p_sigma - P_t)^2 is in the Metropolis kernel (`perimeter_energy_delta`, L199-206; `dp_old`/`dp_new` parity bookkeeping and acceptance, L560-588) with zero drift against a full recount, lambda_P = 0 reproduces the Pass 2 lattice bit-for-bit, and at lambda_P = 2 RMS(p - P_t) falls 14.05 -> 1.73 bonds, fragmentation 0.217 -> 0.083 and shape index 13.27 -> 12.30 while sorting survives (Delta_r = +0.355 vs +0.332). Three new Lean theorems (0 sorrys) pin the target perimeter 12 s - 4, the single-copy perimeter parity and cost identities, and the monotonicity of the term above P_t. The re-read of the kernel, however, finds defects the v1/v2 assessors missed: a whole-cell `cell_type` identity-swap move with its own Metropolis rule at 2.5 T (L467-500) that is not in the Graner-Glazier formalism, an uncited 1.8 * x lateral bias that manufactures the 'lens' regime (L494-497; A2 is a concentric core-shell, Delta_r = +0.352), cells at 75.6 % of V_t with 3 cells on a hard v >= 6 floor (L530-531), dead `depinning_prob` code (L451-454), PRL Fig. 3 checkpoints without digitisation provenance, and uncited specimen thresholds (L807-831). Model fidelity, specimen match, morphometric validation and both traceability dimensions are therefore scored lower than in v2. Overall 84.5/100 (faithfulness 82.9, reproducibility 88.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 654cd6fc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 76, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 91, Morphometric validation 85, Source and data traceability 87, Code-to-model traceability 83, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/cellular_potts_cell_sorting_comparison.png: rendered output of 1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py at 654cd6fc, image/png, 844973 B, 3000×1890 px, artifact_sha256 a2f5372c202e946ae397351314585b49d1db212e3088826bfc3b642308249496 (sha256 a2f5372c202e946ae397351314585b49d1db212e3088826bfc3b642308249496), spec_fingerprint 7cdd3f38f0e6192e614f25f3f47d81cb4d09870705b0e0dca1d1d4dbca9f4cc0. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 7cdd3f38f0e6192e614f25f3f47d81cb4d09870705b0e0dca1d1d4dbca9f4cc0; artifact_sha256: a2f5372c202e946ae397351314585b49d1db212e3088826bfc3b642308249496. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Graner & Glazier (1992) PRL Eqs. 1-3 & Fig. 3: extended large-Q Cellular Potts Model Hamiltonian with bond-energy surface tensions gamma_LD = J_LD - (J_LL + J_DD)/2 and gamma_alphaM = J_alphaM - J_alphaalpha/2 driving logarithmic heterotypic boundary decay L_het(t) ~ A - B ln(t). | Glazier & Graner (1993) PRE Table I & Section III.B: classification of 4 equilibrium phase regimes (complete engulfment, partial sorting lens, checkerboard mixing, and cell dissociation) and fluctuation temperature controls (T=0 lattice pinning arrest vs optimal thermal sorting vs high-T thermal melting). | Ouchi et al. (2003) Physica A Eq. 2: a perimeter (cortical tension) elasticity term lambda_P (p_sigma - P_t)^2 added to the CPM Hamiltonian suppresses ragged, fragmented cell boundaries; Farhadifar et al. (2007) Eq. 1 is the vertex-model analogue.; reconstructed_in_script: 2D extended large-Q Cellular Potts Model (60 x 60 lattice, 60 cells of V_t = 16) across all 4 canonical phase regimes plus T=0 pinning and equal-adhesion negative controls, a 7-point continuous J_LD sweep, and a 6-point fluctuation temperature sweep (all at lambda_P = 0). | Ouchi et al. (2003) perimeter / cortical tension term with incremental 8-neighbour bond-count bookkeeping (max drift 0 after 150 MCS), a cortical-tension sorting regime (lambda_P = 2, P_t = 44), a 6-point lambda_P ablation sweep at T = 10 and T = 80, and a 5-point P_t sweep (32-56) with realised-perimeter tracking r = 0.9999. | Computer-vision segmentation of a confocal fluorescence embryonic cell aggregate (`embryonic_cell_aggregate_specimen.jpg`) comparing empirical GFP/RFP radial occupancy against CPM core-shell profiles (r = 0.961, RMSE = 0.154).; transfer_boundary: 2D lattice Cellular Potts representation of 3D multicellular spheroid cross-sections; the specimen is an embryoid-body spheroid, not a Hydra reaggregate, and its core/shell labels are assigned by fluorescence channel, not by cell type. | Sorting dynamics include a whole-cell identity-swap move (8 attempts/MCS, Metropolis at 2.5 T) that is not part of the Graner-Glazier single-site copy formalism; the 'partial sorting lens' regime adds an uncited lateral bias field inside that move. Both are disclosed here, not in the script. | Cells equilibrate at ~76 % of V_t under lambda = 1.2 and a hard v >= 6 floor; the PRL Fig. 3 comparison uses 0-150 MCS checkpoints whose digitisation from the 10^4-MCS figure is not documented.; does_not_claim: Does not model subcellular cytoskeletal actin-myosin turnover, active chemotactic signaling, cell growth/division, or 3D aggregates; does not reproduce Glazier & Graner (1993) quantitative boundary-length curves at the paper's cell size (V_t ~ 40) or run length (10^4 MCS).." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py:369, 530-531 — cells equilibrate at mean v = 12.1 (75.6 % of V_t = 16, RMS 5.16, 3 cells on the hard `vols <= 6` floor) because lambda = 1.2 is weak against J ~ 14-16. Raise lambda (or rescale J) so mean v is within 5 % of V_t as in Glazier & Graner (1993), remove the extra-Hamiltonian floor, add a lambda sweep panel and expose mean_vol / V_t as a measurement with reference 1.0.",
        "remediation needed: 1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py:451-454 — `depinning_prob` is computed and never used; delete it or use it, and rewrite the §III.B comment so the documented pinning mechanism is the one the acceptance rule (L575-579) actually implements.",
        "remediation needed: 1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py:467-500 — remove the whole-cell `cell_type` identity-swap move (8 attempts/MCS, Metropolis at 2.5 T) or demote it to an explicitly labelled non-GGH accelerator behind a CLI flag defaulting to off; sorting must then arise from single-site copies alone (raise n_mcs and/or T as needed) and the self-test must assert Delta_r > 0.25 with swaps disabled. Report the swap-free Delta_r as a measurement so the Hamiltonian's own sorting power is attributable.",
        "remediation needed: 1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py:469, 494-497 and 932-936 — the `is_partial` 1.8 * x lateral bias field is uncited and the resulting A2 panel is a concentric core-shell (Delta_r = +0.352 > A1), not Glazier & Graner's lens doublet. Delete the bias, seed the lens regime as two apposed homotypic half-aggregates (as the PRE does) and add a lens morphometric (centroid offset / interface curvature) with a reference from PRE Table I or Fig. 6.",
        "remediation needed: 1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py:807-831 — cite or derive the specimen segmentation constants (0.35 channel-bleed subtraction, 82nd / 42nd percentile thresholds, r_roi = 88 px, panel crop boxes) in the dataset README/JSON and add a sensitivity check (e.g. thresholds ±5 percentiles) to the self-test so the r = 0.961 profile match is shown to be robust.",
        "remediation needed: 1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py:926-961 — the canonical A/B panels are still rendered at lambda_P = 0 and show 21.7 % fragmented cells; once the volume constraint is fixed, run the lambda_P sweep across all four regimes (not only the complete-sorting J set) and report whether the Ouchi term changes the regime boundaries of Panel B2.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/cellular_potts_cell_sorting/cellular_potts_cell_sorting_reference.json:169-180 and 1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py:868-878 — the PRL Fig. 3 `empirical_mcs_checkpoints` (0-150 MCS) have no digitisation provenance; the paper's figure spans ~10^4 MCS for V_t ~ 40 cells. Either digitise Fig. 3 (record axis ranges, tool and rescaling) or relabel the checkpoints as a synthetic target and drop the 'Fig. 3 checkpoint concordance' language from the measurement, panel B1 and the audit summary." ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.45e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-parameter-expressivity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Graner & Glazier (1992) / Glazier & Graner (1993) extended large-Q Cellular Potts Model cell sorting + Ouchi et al. (2003) cortical tension — Parameter expressivity: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: six regimes (A1-A5 + cortical tension C1), a 7-point J_LD sweep spanning gamma_LD in [-4, +9] (L630-662, Panel B2), a 6-point temperature sweep T in {0, 1.5, 5, 10, 25, 80} (L665-695, Panel B5), and the new Pass 3 sweeps: lambda_P in {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, 4} at T = 10 and T = 80 (L702-741, Panels C2/C5), P_t in {32, 38, 44, 50, 56} at lambda_P = 2 (L744-777, Panel C4) with realised mean perimeter tracking P_t to within 2 bonds (r = 0.9999) and the shape index rising monotonically; CLI exposes every J, V_t, lambda, T, MCS, seed plus the new --lam-P and --Pt (L1505-1523). Deductions: lambda (volume multiplier) is never swept although it is the parameter whose weakness produces the 76 % volume deficit (-4); the lambda_P sweep is run only at the complete-sorting J set, so the term's effect on the checkerboard and dissociation regimes is untested (-3); grid size and cell count are fixed (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-parameter-expressivity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-parameter-expressivity-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-repro-package> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Graner & Glazier (1992) / Glazier & Graner (1993) extended large-Q Cellular Potts Model cell sorting + Ouchi et al. (2003) cortical tension — Reproducibility package: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: deterministic RNG (seed 1992) with a two-run bitwise determinism check (self-test 7) and a bit-for-bit lambda_P = 0 regression against the Pass 2 kernel (check 9); the 12-check `self_test()` (L1394-1501) covers SHA-256, exact tension parity across 5 regimes, sorting vs controls, T = 0 arrest, log decay, specimen correlation, the 15-measurement contract, perimeter definition (4 x 4 = 44, 3 x 3 = 32), zero bookkeeping drift, shape regularisation, lambda_P monotonicity and P_t tracking; `--self-test` runs in ~23 s and the default render in ~20 s, producing the PNG and GIF; `--lam-P` and `--Pt` are documented in argparse and the main() summary prints every headline number. Deductions: no requirements lock file pins numpy/scipy/matplotlib versions (-3); matplotlib emits a font-cache warning when MPLCONFIGDIR is unset, which the invocation notes do not mention (-1); the v2 audit's '<2 s self-test' claim is now 23 s and the README section for this script was not updated in this loop (out of scope for the slot) (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-repro-package-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-repro-package-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-source-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Graner & Glazier (1992) / Glazier & Graner (1993) extended large-Q Cellular Potts Model cell sorting + Ouchi et al. (2003) cortical tension — Source and data traceability: 87/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: `datasets/cellular_potts_cell_sorting/` carries 7 sources with DOIs (JSON L6-46), the SHA-256-pinned specimen with Wikimedia source URL and CC BY 3.0 licence (L47-58), the Pass 3 `perimeter_constraint_extension_ouchi_2003` block (L181-213) with the term, perimeter definition, square-block formula, sweep values, expected behaviour and Lean theorem names, `paper_citations.bib` with 7 entries, and a README that lists the Pass 3 additions; runtime SHA-256 verification is fail-closed (L85-102). Deductions: the two Pass 3 DOIs (Ouchi 2003, Farhadifar 2007) were recorded from memory and are flagged `doi_verification` but not resolved (-3); the Fig. 3 checkpoints (L169-180) cite 'PRL Fig. 3; PRE Figs. 8-10' with no digitisation method, axis rescaling or page (-4); the specimen segmentation constants — 82nd / 42nd percentile thresholds, 0.35 channel-bleed factor, r_roi = 88 px, panel crop boxes — are uncited and undocumented in the dataset (-3); the canonical J set (14, 2, 11, 16, 16), V_t = 16 and lambda = 1.2 are not traced to the paper's own values (the PRL used larger cells and different J magnitudes) (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py L807–L831: Uncited specimen thresholds: 0.35 channel bleed, 82nd / 42nd percentiles, r_roi = 88 px <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py#L807-L831>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-source-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-source-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-source-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.7e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-specimen-match> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Graner & Glazier (1992) / Glazier & Graner (1993) extended large-Q Cellular Potts Model cell sorting + Ouchi et al. (2003) cortical tension — Morphological realism / specimen match: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: the SHA-256-locked confocal embryoid-body specimen is segmented into a GFP core (r_D/R = 0.49) and RFP shell (r_L/R = 0.77, Delta_r = +0.28) and its 12-annulus occupancy profile matches the CPM complete-sorting profile (r = 0.961, RMSE = 0.154, Panel B4); Panel C1 shows visibly more compact, simply connected cells than A1 with the same core-shell topology, and the GIF's fourth column shows the same. Deductions: the A2 'Partial Sorting / Lens' panel is visually indistinguishable from A1 (both concentric core-shells; A2 Delta_r = +0.352 exceeds A1's +0.332) whereas Glazier & Graner's lens regime is a side-by-side doublet (-6); A1 at lambda_P = 0 shows 21.7 % of cells fragmented into satellite pixels, a lattice artefact the paper's larger cells (V_t ~ 40) do not show, and the canonical panels are still rendered at lambda_P = 0 (-4); the specimen is an embryoid-body spheroid labelled by fluorescence channel, not a Hydra endoderm/ectoderm reaggregate, so the core-shell correspondence to cell type is assumed (-4); the specimen comparison uses a 12-bin profile of a single image with no second specimen or Foty et al. (1996) envelopment measurement (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py L932–L936: partial_sorting_lens regime rendered as Panel A2; realised Delta_r = +0.352 > A1, not a lens doublet <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/1992-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting.py#L932-L936>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-specimen-match-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

